{"name":"Bee Cluster","hex":"#ffaa33","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Byangsi."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flying insect, of the clade Anthophila within the hymenopteran superfamily Apoidea, known for its organised societies (though only a minority have them), for collecting pollen and (in some species) producing wax and honey.","Any stinging flying insect, especially a wasp."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bee"},{"term":"cluster","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bunch or group of several discrete items that are close to each other.","A group of galaxies, nebulae, or stars that appear to the naked eye to be near each other."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To collect (animals, people, objects, data points, etc) into clusters (noun sense 1).\n\nTo cover (with clusters); to scatter or strew in clusters (within); to distribute (objects) within such that they form clusters.","To collect (animals, people, objects, data points, etc) into clusters (noun sense 1)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cluster"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bee","blocks":[{"text":"Bees are winged insects that form a monophyletic clade Anthophila within the superfamily Apoidea of the order Hymenoptera, with over 20,000 known species in seven recognized families. Some species – including honey bees, bumblebees, and stingless bees – are social insects living in colonies, whereas over 90% of bee species – including mason bees, carpenter bees, leafcutter bees, and sweat bees – are solitary."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Tetragonula_carbonaria_%2814521993792%29.jpg/330px-Tetragonula_carbonaria_%2814521993792%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bee","wikidata":"Q7391"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm